 Use `waydroid prop set`, not `[properties]` (that entry is refused). Running apps pick up the change on their
 next decoder; `logcat -s nvc2` shows the service's log.
+
+## Shared folders
+
+```ini
+[waydroid]
+shared_folders = ~/Downloads:Download/Host
+    ~/Pictures:Pictures/Host
+```
+
+One `host folder:storage path` pair per line; the storage path is relative to internal storage (`/sdcard`).
+Without the key `~/Downloads` appears as `Download/Host`; `shared_folders =` shares nothing. Android apps may
+create a file only below a standard top-level folder that takes its type (`Download` takes every type, `Pictures`
+and `DCIM` take images and videos), so put storage paths below one. The folders must belong to the session user.
+The container manager mounts them once Android has booted and unmounts them when the container stops; changes take
+effect at the next session start. Files Android creates belong to the session user on the host. Host files appear
+in file managers and the system file picker right away; galleries list them only after MediaStore scanned them.
-- 
